+++ 현행소스/licenses/OCR/ubuntu-gcc/debian27/changelog
@@ -0,0 +1,761 @@
+gcc-mingw-w64 (27) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  [ Konstantin Demin ]
+  * Switch to GCC 14. Closes: #1092654.
+
+  [ Stephen Kitt ]
+  * Use versioned gnat binaries by adding links to their default
+    equivalents in a local directory. This allows the build to use a
+    gnat-... package without depending on the default gnat package.
+  * Drop references to gnatfind and gnatxref, removed in GCC 12.
+  * Standards-Version 4.7.2, no change required.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Sun, 02 Mar 2025 20:11:13 +0100
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.8) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Limit the gnat-mingw-w64-ucrt64 architectures to those where gnat is
+    available.
+  * Add missing Replaces/Conflicts between the bootstrap and regular
+    C/C++ compiler packages. Closes: #1093747.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Fri, 07 Feb 2025 07:51:32 +0100
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.7) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Refactor flag construction, drop --as-needed for the host since
+    that’s the toolchain default.
+  * Always build the bootstrap package.
+  * Remove build directories once they’re installed to reduce disk space
+    requirements.
+  * Make the bootstrap package ship its own documentation instead of
+    depending on the base package. This simplifies dependency resolution
+    for the package in experimental, and means the base package can be
+    dropped in stage1.
+  * Provide UCRT cross-compilers, targeting POSIX threads to match Fedora
+    and MSYS2. Closes: #1038210.
+  * Include stdlib.h in rtinit for gnat.
+  * d/rules: $(COMMA) isn’t defined, use $(comma) instead.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Sat, 18 Jan 2025 18:54:00 +0100
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.6) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * When adjusting parallelism to limit per-CPU memory usage, clamp the
+    result between 1 and the number of available CPUs inclusive. Thanks
+    to Santiago Vila for the patch! Closes: #1088874.
+  * Evaluate flags when declaring them. This fixes the build with Make
+    4.4.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Wed, 04 Dec 2024 07:36:40 +0100
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.5) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * libgfortran doesn’t handle _FOR_TARGET flags, so explicitly set
+    FCFLAGS to the target flags, and avoid using dh_auto_configure so
+    that the flags variables aren’t reset.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Wed, 23 Oct 2024 13:20:10 +0200
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.4) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  [ Konstantin Demin ]
+  * Remove obsolete variables and dh_gencontrol flags.
+  * Handle spaces in spelling fixes correctly.
+  * Simplify version variable construction.
+  * Verbose debhelper by default.
+
+  [ Stephen Kitt ]
+  * Simplify bootstrap handling in debian/rules.
+  * Switch to short dh rules, bumping to debhelper compatibility level
+    10.
+  * Stop requiring the runtime packages in the stage1 profile.
+  * d/rules: consistently use expected/actual argument order in
+    ifeq/ifneq.
+  * When cleaning up runtime .install files, check for ADA in the list
+    of languages, not the arches.
+  * Rely on the build profile to “filter” debian/control.
+  * Standards-Version 4.7.0, no change required.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Sat, 19 Oct 2024 20:09:27 +0200
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.3) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Give an absolute path to debian/changelog as a reference for touch.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Mon, 18 Mar 2024 06:38:05 +0100
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.2) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Never undefine _REENTRANT; this ensures it’s always defined when
+    appropriate (and only when appropriate). Closes: #792909.
+  * Don’t treat missing function declarations as errors when building
+    for Windows, the 64-bit time_t change is irrelevant there. Closes:
+    #1066350.
+  * As suggested by Konstantin Demin, reset the timestamp on BASE-VER
+    after changing it to avoid unwanted rebuilds.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Sun, 17 Mar 2024 23:20:17 +0100
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26.1) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Add missing find arguments...
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Sun, 24 Sep 2023 20:34:25 +0200
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (26) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Switch to GCC 13.
+  * Drop breaks/conflicts for old package splits, the affected versions
+    are all obsolete.
+  * Use find -exec instead of piping find’s output into xargs.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Sat, 23 Sep 2023 18:22:52 +0200
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (25.3) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Stop setting the build timestamp manually, ld takes care of that
+    itself now. Closes: #1052220.
+
+ -- Stephen Kitt <skitt@debian.org>  Thu, 21 Sep 2023 07:23:25 +0200
+
+gcc-mingw-w64 (25.2) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  [ Konstantin Demin ]
+  * Restore the ability to parallel-install POSIX and Win32 thread
